@apiUrl = http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/v1

### 1. Get all cats
GET {{apiUrl}}/cats

### 2. Get cat by ID
GET {{apiUrl}}/cats/1

### 3. Get cats by owner ID (Assignment 5 Requirement 4)
GET {{apiUrl}}/cats/owner/1

### 4. Update a cat
PUT {{apiUrl}}/cats/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cat_name": "Frank Modified",
  "weight": 6.0,
  "owner": 1,
  "birthdate": "2020-04-15"
}

### 5. Delete a cat
DELETE {{apiUrl}}/cats/2

### -------------------------------------------

### 6. Get all users
GET {{apiUrl}}/users

### 7. Get user by ID
GET {{apiUrl}}/users/1

### 8. Add a new user
POST {{apiUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alice Smith",
  "username": "alicesmith",
  "email": "alice@metropolia.fi",
  "role": "user",
  "password": "securepassword"
}

### 9. Update a user
PUT {{apiUrl}}/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Updated",
  "email": "john_updated@example.com"
}

### 10. Delete a user
DELETE {{apiUrl}}/users/2

### -------------------------------------------

### 11. Upload a new cat with an image (Multer multipart/form-data)
POST {{apiUrl}}/cats
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=MyBoundary

--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="cat_name"

Misu
--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="weight"

6
--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="owner"

1
--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="birthdate"

2023-10-08
--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="cat"; filename="dog.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./dog.jpg
--MyBoundary--